  "body": "## What\n\nThe release workflow's `publish` job now writes a `SHA256SUMS.txt` covering every release asset and uploads it with the other files.\n\n- A new step runs `sha256sum` in `dist/` over the same file patterns the job already publishes (zip, setup.exe, tar.gz, deb, rpm, dmg, AppImage, snap, flatpak, pkg.tar.zst), checks the result with `sha256sum -c`, and prints it to the log.\n- `dist/SHA256SUMS.txt` is added to the `softprops/action-gh-release` file list.\n\nThe file uses standard `sha256sum` format (`<hash>  <filename>`), so users can verify a download with:\n\n```\nsha256sum -c --ignore-missing SHA256SUMS.txt\n```\n\n## Why\n\nI've asked for CamCraft to be added to ArtCraft Launcher as a community app (storytold/craft-launcher#1545). The launcher checks every download, including downloads of community apps, against the release's `SHA256SUMS.txt`, so CamCraft can't be listed until its releases include one. Checksums also help anyone who downloads the files by hand.\n\nReleases that are already published don't change. The file will appear starting with the next tag.\n\n## Testing\n\n- The YAML parses.\n- I ran the step's script on sample files: it lists each asset once, `sha256sum -c` passes, and `release-body.md` isn't included.\n- I haven't run it in a real release. That will happen on the next tag.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
